## Task Creation & Modification

### 6. Add Task (`add-task`)

*   **CLI Command:** `npx task-master add-task [options]`
*   **Description:** `Add a new task to Taskmaster by describing it; AI will structure it.`
*   **Key CLI Options:**
    *   `-p, --prompt <text>`: `Required. Describe the new task you want Taskmaster to create, e.g., "Implement user authentication using JWT".`
    *   `-d, --dependencies <ids>`: `Specify the IDs of any Taskmaster tasks that must be completed before this new one can start, e.g., '12,14'.`
    *   `--priority <priority>`: `Set the priority for the new task: 'high', 'medium', or 'low'. Default is 'medium'.`
    *   `-r, --research`: `Enable Taskmaster to use the research role for potentially more informed task creation.`
    *   `-f, --file <file>`: `Path to your Taskmaster 'tasks.json' file. Default relies on auto-detection.`
*   **Usage:** Quickly add newly identified tasks during development.
*   **Important:** This command makes AI calls and can take up to a minute to complete. Please inform users to hang tight while the operation is in progress.

### 7. Add Subtask (`add-subtask`)

*   **CLI Command:** `npx task-master add-subtask [options]`
*   **Description:** `Add a new subtask to a Taskmaster parent task, or convert an existing task into a subtask.`
*   **Key CLI Options:**
    *   `-p, --parent <id>`: `Required. The ID of the Taskmaster task that will be the parent.`
    *   `-i, --task-id <id>`: `Use this if you want to convert an existing top-level Taskmaster task into a subtask of the specified parent.`
    *   `-t, --title <title>`: `Required if not using taskId. The title for the new subtask Taskmaster should create.`
    *   `-d, --description <text>`: `A brief description for the new subtask.`
    *   `--details <text>`: `Provide implementation notes or details for the new subtask.`
    *   `--dependencies <ids>`: `Specify IDs of other tasks or subtasks, e.g., '15' or '16.1', that must be done before this new subtask.`
    *   `-s, --status <status>`: `Set the initial status for the new subtask. Default is 'pending'.`
    *   `--skip-generate`: `Prevent Taskmaster from automatically regenerating markdown task files after adding the subtask.`
    *   `-f, --file <file>`: `Path to your Taskmaster 'tasks.json' file. Default relies on auto-detection.`
*   **Usage:** Break down tasks manually or reorganize existing tasks.

### 8. Update Tasks (`update`)

*   **CLI Command:** `npx task-master update [options]`
*   **Description:** `Update multiple upcoming tasks in Taskmaster based on new context or changes, starting from a specific task ID.`
*   **Key CLI Options:**
    *   `--from <id>`: `Required. The ID of the first task Taskmaster should update. All tasks with this ID or higher that are not 'done' will be considered.`
    *   `-p, --prompt <text>`: `Required. Explain the change or new context for Taskmaster to apply to the tasks, e.g., "We are now using React Query instead of Redux Toolkit for data fetching".`
    *   `-r, --research`: `Enable Taskmaster to use the research role for more informed updates. Requires appropriate API key.`
    *   `-f, --file <file>`: `Path to your Taskmaster 'tasks.json' file. Default relies on auto-detection.`
*   **Usage:** Handle significant implementation changes or pivots that affect multiple future tasks. Example CLI: `npx task-master update --from='18' --prompt='Switching to React Query.\nNeed to refactor data fetching...'`
*   **Important:** This command makes AI calls and can take up to a minute to complete. Please inform users to hang tight while the operation is in progress.

### 9. Update Task (`update-task`)

*   **CLI Command:** `npx task-master update-task [options]`
*   **Description:** `Modify a specific Taskmaster task or subtask by its ID, incorporating new information or changes.`
*   **Key CLI Options:**
    *   `-i, --id <id>`: `Required. The specific ID of the Taskmaster task, e.g., '15', or subtask, e.g., '15.2', you want to update.`
    *   `-p, --prompt <text>`: `Required. Explain the specific changes or provide the new information Taskmaster should incorporate into this task.`
    *   `-r, --research`: `Enable Taskmaster to use the research role for more informed updates. Requires appropriate API key.`
    *   `-f, --file <file>`: `Path to your Taskmaster 'tasks.json' file. Default relies on auto-detection.`
*   **Usage:** Refine a specific task based on new understanding or feedback. Example CLI: `npx task-master update-task --id='15' --prompt='Clarification: Use PostgreSQL instead of MySQL.\nUpdate schema details...'`
*   **Important:** This command makes AI calls and can take up to a minute to complete. Please inform users to hang tight while the operation is in progress.

### 10. Update Subtask (`update-subtask`)

*   **CLI Command:** `npx task-master update-subtask [options]`
*   **Description:** `Append timestamped notes or details to a specific Taskmaster subtask without overwriting existing content. Intended for iterative implementation logging.`
*   **Key CLI Options:**
    *   `-i, --id <id>`: `Required. The specific ID of the Taskmaster subtask, e.g., '15.2', you want to add information to.`
    *   `-p, --prompt <text>`: `Required. Provide the information or notes Taskmaster should append to the subtask's details. Ensure this adds *new* information not already present.`
    *   `-r, --research`: `Enable Taskmaster to use the research role for more informed updates. Requires appropriate API key.`
    *   `-f, --file <file>`: `Path to your Taskmaster 'tasks.json' file. Default relies on auto-detection.`
*   **Usage:** Add implementation notes, code snippets, or clarifications to a subtask during development. Before calling, review the subtask's current details to append only fresh insights, helping to build a detailed log of the implementation journey and avoid redundancy. Example CLI: `npx task-master update-subtask --id='15.2' --prompt='Discovered that the API requires header X.\nImplementation needs adjustment...'`
*   **Important:** This command makes AI calls and can take up to a minute to complete. Please inform users to hang tight while the operation is in progress.

### 11. Set Task Status (`set-status`)

*   **CLI Command:** `npx task-master set-status [options]`
*   **Description:** `Update the status of one or more Taskmaster tasks or subtasks, e.g., 'pending', 'in-progress', 'done'.`
*   **Key CLI Options:**
    *   `-i, --id <id>`: `Required. The ID(s) of the Taskmaster task(s) or subtask(s), e.g., '15', '15.2', or '16,17.1', to update.`
    *   `-s, --status <status>`: `Required. The new status to set, e.g., 'done', 'pending', 'in-progress', 'review', 'cancelled'.`
    *   `-f, --file <file>`: `Path to your Taskmaster 'tasks.json' file. Default relies on auto-detection.`
*   **Usage:** Mark progress as tasks move through the development cycle.

### 12. Remove Task (`remove-task`)

*   **CLI Command:** `npx task-master remove-task [options]`
*   **Description:** `Permanently remove a task or subtask from the Taskmaster tasks list.`
*   **Key CLI Options:**
    *   `-i, --id <id>`: `Required. The ID of the Taskmaster task, e.g., '5', or subtask, e.g., '5.2', to permanently remove.`
    *   `-y, --yes`: `Skip the confirmation prompt and immediately delete the task.`
    *   `-f, --file <file>`: `Path to your Taskmaster 'tasks.json' file. Default relies on auto-detection.`
*   **Usage:** Permanently delete tasks or subtasks that are no longer needed in the project.
*   **Notes:** Use with caution as this operation cannot be undone. Consider using 'blocked', 'cancelled', or 'deferred' status instead if you just want to exclude a task from active planning but keep it for reference. The command automatically cleans up dependency references in other tasks.

